{"abstract":"Machine learning (ML) benchmarks are crucial for evaluating the performance, efficiency, and scalability of ML systems, especially as the adoption of complex ML pipelines, such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), continues to grow. These pipelines introduce intricate execution graphs that require more advanced benchmarking approaches. Additionally, collocating workloads can improve resource efficiency but may introduce contention challenges that must be carefully managed. Detailed insights into resource utilization are necessary for effective collocation and optimized edge deployments. However, existing benchmarking frameworks often fail to capture these critical aspects.We introduce a modular end-to-end ML benchmarking framework designed to address these gaps. Our framework emphasizes modularity and reusability by enabling reusable pipeline stages, facilitating flexible benchmarking across diverse ML workflows. It supports complex workloads and measures their end-to-end performance. The workloads can be collocated, with the framework providing insights into resource utilization and contention between the concurrent workloads.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bayer, Robert","Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818243"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmarking","Deep learning","Edge computing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a modular end to end machine learning benchmarking framework","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3719159.3721223","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818243","identifier":[{"id":"105003119925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7702f384-2591-4960-abce-f443e9eac67d"],"keyword":["Benchmarking","Deep Learning","Edge Computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A776E7A4C0A5304F8C95A70568919C38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3719159.3721223","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://robertbayer.github.io/publication/towards-modular-benchmark/towards-modular-benchmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Resource-Aware Data Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"bayerpau","last":"Bayer","locid":"71115e9d-836f-409e-8c75-27d2de3e9caa","name":"Bayer, Robert","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-7702f384-2591-4960-abce-f443e9eac67d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards A Modular End-To-End Machine Learning Benchmarking Framework","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818243","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Antibiotic treatments have detrimental effects on the microbiome and lead to antibiotic resistance. To develop a phage therapy against a diverse range of clinically relevant Escherichia coli, we screened a library of 162 wild-type (WT) phages, identifying eight phages with broad coverage of E. coli, complementary binding to bacterial surface receptors, and the capability to stably carry inserted cargo. Selected phages were engineered with tail fibers and CRISPR–Cas machinery to specifically target E. coli. We show that engineered phages target bacteria in biofilms, reduce the emergence of phage-tolerant E. coli and out-compete their ancestral WT phages in coculture experiments. A combination of the four most complementary bacteriophages, called SNIPR001, is well tolerated in both mouse models and minipigs and reduces E. coli load in the mouse gut better than its constituent components separately. SNIPR001 is in clinical development to selectively kill E. coli, which may cause fatal infections in hematological cancer patients.","author_count":36,"contributors":["Gencay, Yilmaz Emre","Jasinskytė, Džiuginta","Robert, Camille","Semsey, Szabolcs","Martínez, Virginia","Petersen, Anders Østergaard","Brunner, Katja","de Santiago Torio, Ana","Salazar, Alex","Turcu, Iszabela Cristiana","Eriksen, Melissa Kviesgaard","Koval, Lev","Takos, Adam","Pascal, Ricardo","Schou, Thea Staffeldt","Bayer, Lone","Bryde, Tina","Johansen, Katja Chandelle","Bak, Emilie Glad","Smrekar, Frenk","Doyle, Timothy B.","Satlin, Michael J.","Gram, Aurelie","Carvalho, Joana","Jessen, Lene","Hallström, Björn","Hink, Jonas","Damholt, Birgitte","Troy, Alice","Grove, Mette","Clube, Jasper","Grøndahl, Christian","Haaber, Jakob Krause","van der Helm, Eric","Zdravkovic, Milan","Sommer, Morten Otto Alexander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-775403"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sommer, Morten Otto Alexander"],"country":["Slovenia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","JAFRAL","JMI Laboratories"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engineered phage with antibacterial crispr cas selectively reduce e coli burden in mice","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41587-023-01759-y","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["All authors affiliated with SNIPR Biome are present or past employees of SNIPR Biome and maybe share- or warrant holders. F.S. and T.B.D. are subcontractors of SNIPR Biome. M.J.S. received research funding from Merck, Biomérieux and SNIPR Biome. M.J.S. is an unpaid consultant for SNIPR Biome and has been consulting for Shionogi and participated on a Data Safety Monitoring Board for AbbVie. Patent applications have been filed based on material described in this article. SNIPR, CRISPR-Guided Vectors and CGV are trademarks of SNIPR Biome ApS. Data not included in the publication is commercially sensitive as SNIPR Biome is in the process of securing patent protection for these aspects, which precludes their inclusion in the paper at this stage. Upon request, SNIPR Biome is willing to share all data with other parties with no competing interest. SNIPR Biome acknowledges funding from Combating Antibiotic-Resistant Bacteria Biopharmaceutical Accelerator (CARB-X). Research reported in this publication is supported by CARB-X. CARB-X’s funding for this project is sponsored by the Cooperative Agreement Number IDSEP160030 from ASPR/BARDA and by an award from Wellcome Trust. The content is solely the responsibility of the authors and does not necessarily represent the official views of CARB-X or any of its funders. We would also like to thank our collaborators at SSI (Denmark) and Minerva Imaging (Denmark) for their contribution to the manuscript. We would like to acknowledge E. Søndberg (SNIPR BIOME) who illustrated Fig. ."],"id":"S01-000.00-775403","identifier":[{"id":"37142704","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10869271","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85158118682","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5a10b497-c2ad-48ba-a3b2-d9f1bb2e0cee"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FEC569D20A143738C1B21583968862F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/381826180/s41587-023-01759-y_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41587-023-01759-y","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["SNIPR Biome Aps"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"si","key":"jafral","loc":["Slovenia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"JAFRAL","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"jmi laboratories","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"JMI Laboratories","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability","Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Founda