:"37","corresponding":null,"first":"Arjan C.","key":"lankesterpau","last":"Lankester","name":"Lankester, Arjan C.","rank":52,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mary","key":"slatterpau","last":"Slatter","name":"Slatter, Mary","rank":53,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jennifer A.","key":"kanakrypau","last":"Kanakry","name":"Kanakry, Jennifer A.","rank":54,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34033842"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jaci.2021.04.036","issn":["00916749","10858725"],"issn_org":["00916749"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Allergy and Clinical Immunology","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Allergy and Clinical Immunology","volume":"149"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108088207"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-86098270-b9a4-410d-a53a-83eb9b1f7879"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"International retrospective study of allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation for activated PI3K-delta syndrome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-205849","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Despite their resource- and power-constrained nature, edge devices also exhibit an increase in the available compute and memory resources and heterogeneity, similar to the evolution of server hardware in the past decade. For example, NVIDIA Jetson devices have a system-on-chip (SoC) composed of an ARM CPU and an NVIDIA GPU sharing RAM that could be up to 32 GB. Such an SoC setup offers opportunities to push down complex computations closer to the data source rather than performing them on remote servers. In this paper, we characterize the performance of two types of NVIDIA Jetson devices for end-to-end machine learning pipelines using the TPCx-AI benchmark. Our results demonstrate that the available memory is the main limitation to performance and scaling up machine learning workloads on edge devices. Despite this limitation, some edge devices show promise when comparing against a desktop hardware in terms of power-efficiency and reduction in data movement. In addition, exploiting the available compute parallelism on these devices can benefit not just model training and inference but also data pre-processing. By parallelizing, we get close to an order of magnitude improvement in pre-processing time for one of the TPCx-AI use cases. Finally, while TPCx-AI is a valuable benchmark, it is designed for server settings; therefore, the community needs an end-to-end machine learning benchmark targeting IoT/edge.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bayer, Robert","Tøttrup, Jon Voigt","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695237"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Edge computing","Machine Learning Pipelines","NVIDIA Jetson","System on Chip SoC","TPCx AI Benchmark"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tpcx ai on nvidia jetsons","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102674781/TPCx_AI_on_Jetsons.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695237","identifier":[{"id":"85152539475","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-42c2d3b4-0aa7-447f-ad5e-4cde4c809eeb"],"keyword":["Edge Computing","Machine Learning Pipelines","NVIDIA Jetson","System-on-Chip (SoC)","TPCx-AI Benchmark"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B2E0268E176C98ED144059F7200C109D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102674781/TPCx_AI_on_Jetsons.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/TPCx_AI_on_Jetsons.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"bayerpau","last":"Bayer","locid":"71115e9d-836f-409e-8c75-27d2de3e9caa","name":"Bayer, Robert","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon Voigt","key":"tøttruppau","last":"Tøttrup","name":"Tøttrup, Jon Voigt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-29576-8_4","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"49-66","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"13860"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152539475"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-42c2d3b4-0aa7-447f-ad5e-4cde4c809eeb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"TPCx-AI on NVIDIA Jetsons","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695237","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The drive to achieve greater energy efficiencies is well‐established in the fine chemical industries with distillation processes being a key focus due to their disproportionate energy consumption totaling more than 40% of the overall plant. The objective of this paper is to specifically focus on the energy efficiency benefits that would be realized by employing intensified distillation column configurations on a high purity, multicomponent, high recovery industrial methanol distillation where a middle boiling trace ethanol component must be managed to ensure on specification production (<10 ppm wt. ethanol in product and <5 ppm impurities in bottoms). Based on technology maturity constraints, five column configurations were selected for further analysis, comprising a direct synthesis configuration, a side draw column, a Petlyuk inspired recovery column arrangement, a divided wall column, and a cut divided wall column. These configurations were then simulated on an industrial process simulator where all configurations were able to match the strict industrial product specifications and design limits. The energy usage of the column configurations was improved through a systematic analysis, and the results revealed that all intensified columns have a superior energy usage compared to the direct synthesis configuration but with the gains limited to only 3%. An unbiased consideration of the energy efficiency results, together with other external factors including cost of capital and operability, shows that the recovery column configuration would be the most practical choice despite the presence of the divided wall column configuration which represents a greater level of intensification and integration.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Udugama, Isuru A.","Kirkpatrick, Robert","Yu, Wei","Gernaey, Krist","Young, Brent R.","Bayer, Christoph"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-371030"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Young, Brent R."],"country":["Germany","New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technische Hochschule Nürnberg","The University of Auckland"],"keyword":["Divided wall column","High purity distillation","Multicomponent","Side draw"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"separation of middle boiling trace compounds by distillation an investigation of practical implications of complex column arrangements on an industrial methanol distillation case study","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85092527450","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-371030","identifier":[{"id":"85092527450","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-de348372-d150-42a4-af82-5e652c2afb9a"],"keyword":["Divided wall column","High purity distillation","Middle boiling","Multicomponent","Petlyuk","Side draw","Trace component"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3EB7B3B482C9709BA6F25CB83EF0EAFF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, PROSYS - Process and Systems Engineering Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nz","key":"the university of auckland","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"The University of Auckland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technische hochschule nürnberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technische Hochschule Nürnberg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Isuru A.","key":"udugamapau","last":"Udugama","locid":"fc5bb820-d4f8-4546-b85f-5bd6c673dc8b","name":"Udugama, Isuru A.","orcid":"0000-0003-1597-1208","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"kirkpatrickpau","last":"Kirkpatrick","name":"Kirkpatrick, Robert","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Krist V.","key":"gernaeypau","last":"Gernaey","locid":"cc1a5662-82ba-4420-96be-f2a9d371b22d","name":"Gernaey, Krist","name_org":"Gernaey, Krist V.","orcid":"0000-0002-0364-1773","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Brent R.","key":"youngpau","last":"Young","name":"Young, Brent R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"bayerpau","last":"Bayer","name":"Bayer, Christoph","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/apj.2588","issn":["19322135"],"issue":"16","journal":"Asia-Pacific Journal of Chemical Engineering","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Asia-Pacific Journal of Chemical Engineering","volume":"2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092527450"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-de348372-d150-42a4-af82-5e652c2afb9a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Separation of middle boiling trace compounds by distillation: An investigation of practical implications of complex column arrangements on an industrial methanol distillation case study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-371030","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Process integration in distillation unit operations promises improved process efficiencies. However, to realize these benefits fit for purpose control structures are needed to ensure stable and on-specification operations. In practice, this requires the development of regulatory and advanced process controls accounting for nuances and intricacies of a given design and application. This manuscript focuses on developing a control structure for a novel industrial mass-integrated twin-column distillation configuration, where a multi-component crude methanol feed is refined into AA grade (ultra-high purity) methanol, while meeting many technical and economic requirements. To this end, a Digital Model (a dynamic process model) of the column configuration was developed and used to carry out a thorough dynamic analysis. Based on the understanding gained, a regulatory control layer was introduced to achieve stable operations. An advanced supervisory level control structure and a Model Predictive Control (MPC) structure were then developed and compared on the Digital model where both alternatives achieved on-specification (technical and economic) operations. It was illustrated that a well-designed control structure could achieve stable and on-specification control for this specific application. Further disturbance testing showed the MPC is marginal efficient than a supervisory control but has similar robustness.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Halager, Niels S.","Bayer, Christoph","Kirkpatrick, Robert","Gernaey, Krist","Huusom, Jakob Kjøbsted","Udugama, Isuru A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-351715"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Huusom, Jakob Kjøbsted"],"country":["Germany","New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technische Hochschule Nürnberg","The University of Auckland"],"keyword":["High purity distillation","Process simulation","Supervisory control"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling and control of an integrated high purity methanol distillation configuration","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cep.2021.108640","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-351715","identifier":[{"id":"85115737642","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9e1763da-840d-4c22-a262-92bf93d851e7"],"keyword":["Grade AA Methanol","High purity distillation","Process simulation","Stabilizing control","Supervisory control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-335D657E99AFF9183ED7136293693E62"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/259040039/1_s2.0_S0255270121003330_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cep.2021.108640","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nz","key":"the university of auckland","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"The University of Auckland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technische hochschule nürnberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technische Hochschule Nürnberg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels S.","key":"halagerpau","last":"Halager","name":"Halager, Niels S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"bayerpau","last":"Bayer","name":"Bayer, Christoph","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"kirkpatrickpau","last":"Kirkpatrick","name":"Kirkpatrick, Robert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Krist V.","key":"gernaeypau","last":"Gernaey","locid":"cc1a5662-82ba-4420-96be-f2a9d371b22d","name":"Gernaey, Krist","name_org":"Gernaey, Krist V.","orcid":"0000-0002-0364-1773","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Kjøbsted","key":"huusompau","last":"Huusom","locid":"0107490a-4116-4fac-ac2c-00ccf7ffe337","name":"Huusom, Jakob Kjøbsted","orcid":"0000-0002-1367-7235","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Isuru A.","key":"udugamapau","last":"Udugama","locid":"fc5bb820-d4f8-4546-b85f-5bd6c673dc8b","name":"Udugama, Isuru A.","orcid":"0000-0003-1597-1208","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cep.2021.108640","issn":["02552701","18733204"],"issn_org":["02552701"],"journal":"Chemical Engineering and Processing - Process Intensification","paperid":"108640","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Chemical Engineering and Processing - Process Intensification","title_org":"Chemical Engineering and Processing","volume":"169"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115737642"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9e1763da-840d-4c22-a262-92bf93d851e7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Modelling and Control of an Integrated High Purity Methanol Distillation Configuration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-351715","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"As the global health crisis unfolded, many academic conferences moved online in 2020. This move has been hailed as a positive step towards inclusivity in its attenuation of economic, physical, and legal barriers and effectively enabled many individuals from groups that have traditionally been underrepresented to join and participate. A number of studies have outlined how moving online made it possible to gather a more global community and has increased opportunities for individuals with various constraints, e.g., caregiving responsibilities. Yet, the mere existence of online conferences is no guarantee that everyone can attend and participate meaningfully. In fact, many elements of an online conference are still significant barriers to truly diverse participation: the tools used can be inaccessible for some individuals; the scheduling choices can favour some geographical locations; the set-up of the conference can provide more visibility to well-established researchers and reduce opportunities for early-career researchers. While acknowledging the benefits of an online setting, especially for individuals who have traditionally been underrepresented or excluded, we recognize that fostering social justice requires inclusivity to actively be centered in every aspect of online conference design. Here, we draw from the literature and from our own experiences to identify practices that purposefully encourage a diverse community to attend, participate in, and lead online conferences. Reflecting on how to design more inclusive online events is especially important as multiple scientific organizations have announced that they will continue offering an online version of their event when in-person conferences can resume.","author_count":109,"contributors":["Levitis, Elizabeth","van Praag, Cassandra D Gould","Gau, Rémi","Heunis, Stephan","DuPre, Elizabeth","Kiar, Gregory","Bottenhorn, Katherine L","Glatard, Tristan","Nikolaidis, Aki","Whitaker, Kirstie Jane","Mancin