tz","name":"Baehtz, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert S.","key":"weatheruppau","last":"Weatherup","name":"Weatherup, Robert S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"schloeglpau","last":"Schloegl","name":"Schloegl, Robert","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernhard C.","key":"bayerpau","last":"Bayer","name":"Bayer, Bernhard C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephan","key":"hofmannpau","last":"Hofmann","name":"Hofmann, Stephan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/cm502603n","issn":["08974756","15205002"],"issn_org":["08974756"],"issue":"22","journal":"Chemistry of Materials","pages":"6380-6392","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Chemistry of Materials","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84912571568"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1de225e4-e264-4f83-b661-935638fe3438"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"In situ observations during chemical vapor deposition of hexagonal boron nitride on polycrystalline copper","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313495","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Diabetes, obesity, and cancer affect upward of 15% of the world's population. Interestingly, all three diseases juxtapose dysregulated intracellular signaling with altered metabolic state. Exactly which genetic factors define stable metabolic set points in vivo remains poorly understood. Here, we show that hedgehog signaling rewires cellular metabolism. We identify a cilium-dependent Smo-Ca(2+)-Ampk axis that triggers rapid Warburg-like metabolic reprogramming within minutes of activation and is required for proper metabolic selectivity and flexibility. We show that Smo modulators can uncouple the Smo-Ampk axis from canonical signaling and identify cyclopamine as one of a new class of \"selective partial agonists,\" capable of concomitant inhibition of canonical and activation of noncanonical hedgehog signaling. Intriguingly, activation of the Smo-Ampk axis in vivo drives robust insulin-independent glucose uptake in muscle and brown adipose tissue. These data identify multiple noncanonical endpoints that are pivotal for rational design of hedgehog modulators and provide a new therapeutic avenue for obesity and diabetes.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Teperino, Raffaele","Amann, Sabine","Bayer, Martina","McGee, Sean L","Loipetzberger, Andrea","Connor, Timothy","Jaeger, Carsten","Kammerer, Bernd","Winter, Lilli","Wiche, Gerhard","Dalgaard, Kevin","Selvaraj, Madhan","Gaster, Michael","Lee-Young, Robert S","Febbraio, Mark A","Knauf, Claude","Cani, Patrice D","Aberger, Fritz","Penninger, Josef M","Pospisilik, J Andrew","Esterbauer, Harald"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-623040"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adipocytes","Adipose Tissue Brown","Animals","Cell Line","Cells Cultured","Cilia","Diabetes mellitus","Glycolysis","Hedgehog Proteins","Humans","Mice","Muscle Cells","Neoplasms","Obesity","Protein Kinases","Receptors G Protein Coupled","Signal Transduction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hedgehog partial agonism drives warburg like metabolism in muscle and brown fat","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.09.021","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-623040","identifier":[{"id":"23063129","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84867536639","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ae010863-76ad-4a7e-b6ef-235bb4afd3f3"],"keyword":["Adipocytes","Adipose Tissue, Brown","Animals","Cell Line","Cells, Cultured","Cilia","Diabetes Mellitus","Glycolysis","Hedgehog Proteins","Humans","Mice","Muscle Cells","Neoplasms","Obesity","Protein Kinases","Receptors, G-Protein-Coupled","Signal Transduction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22E0D4DADEBB31A673277C591D667931"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.09.021","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, KMEB - Molecular Endocrinology Department (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Pathology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Raffaele","key":"teperinopau","last":"Teperino","name":"Teperino, Raffaele","rank":1,"rolecode":